/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2789:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/3/code.py:167:    Eject content pixels from diagonal cup-frames outward along a 45-degree tail direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2790:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/3/code.py:170:    - Detect a corner spike and infer one of four diagonal tail directions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2791:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/3/code.py:173:    - Emit content color diagonally from the spike, but stop before the first non-bg obstacle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2792:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/3/code.py:260:    Build a diagonal funnel whose spike is the NW corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2793:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/3/code.py:337:    Find a placement with a reserved diagonal ray and one obstacle on that ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2794:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/17/code.py:11:#    diagonal partners now share colors in the rotationally symmetric output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2795:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/17/code.py:29:#    - \"one color = one piece\" is false because diagonal partners reuse colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2796:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/17/code.py:42:#    diagonal color pairing and the input often contains same-colored pieces\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2797:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/17/code.py:324:    - Pieces may be rotated or reflected in the input; the anchor specifically may appear as a horizontal or vertical mirror of its output form, and diagonal partners may share colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_com