/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2916:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/16/code.py:533:    \"\"\"Arrange children in a random layout (vertical, horizontal, or diagonal).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2917:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/16/code.py:540:    mode = random.choice((\"vertical\", \"horizontal\", \"diagonal\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2918:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/9/code.py:18:#      anti-diagonal corridor; a 2x2 end block sits in the opposite bg region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2919:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/9/code.py:77:#      least one diagonal bg neighbor so its collision stamp is visually larger\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2920:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/9/code.py:226:            f\"obstacle at ({r},{c}) must have a diagonal bg neighbor for a visible stamp\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2921:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/9/code.py:525:    \"\"\"Return a boolean mask for a thick meandering anti-diagonal band.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2922:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/9/code.py:587:        mode = random.choice((\"vertical\", \"horizontal\", \"diagonal\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2923:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/26/code.py:78:    - using only cardinal arrows avoids mixing the D6 geometric effect with diagonal corner-cutting\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2924:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/19/code.py:10:#       the attached irregular segment is removed, wrapped around the obstacle, and extended diagonally after leaving the skin\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2925:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/19/code.py:22:#       - draw a 7-pixel rerouted path: approach + alongside + diagonal exit tail\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2926:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/19/code.py:26:#       - draw only the visible prefix near the obstacle: the 2 diagonal approach cells plus the 2 straight alongside cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2927:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/19/code.py:32:#     - both approach and alongside are forced to be present, so the new arc is not reducible to a single diagonal or a single straight stub\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2928:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/19/code.py:60:# - the approach+alongside route is at least 3 cells long in raw form and contains both a diagonal run and a straight run\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2929:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/19/code.py:349:    assert first in (\"FL\", \"FR\"), f\"approach must start diagonally, got {first}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2930:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:28:#   3. The marker's whole bbox is translated by one pixel per step along that diagonal,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2931:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:29:#      creating a staircase-like diagonal strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2932:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:35:#     (+1,+1), and the plus disappears in the output. One long diagonal strip may already be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2933:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:39:# - Marker count is constrained to 2-4, matching the four diagonal quadrants. This keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2934:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:41:# - Seed shapes are limited to 1x2 or 2x1. That is deliberate: with one-pixel diagonal shifts,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2935:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:48:#   diagonal marker intentionally contacts two sides. The solver now infers a diagonal from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2936:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:51:#   for diagonal rays. The new extension translates the entire marker bbox by (±1, ±1) each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2937:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:65:#   so acceptance means all chosen diagonal markers are simultaneously legal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2938:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:68:# - A human can see several corner-attached seeds around the same '+', plus one long diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2939:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:69:#   exemplar somewhere in the grid. That makes the diagonal repetition rule and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2940:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:74:# - Generator forbids 4-neighbor contacts between foreign structures, so the diagonal strips do\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2941:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:83:#   preserving only the diagonal strips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2942:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:87:#   horizontal side, which together encode one diagonal quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2943:/h