/21/code.py:33:#      copy of the input frame ratio that can still hold the diagonal child layout with a 1-cell moat.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2972:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:48:#      Invalid now: sibling order depends only on radial distance, so layout becomes a diagonal rank display.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2973:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:53:#      diagonal items.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2974:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:277:    - Inside each frame, sort direct children by increasing centroid distance to the frame center and place them as a down-right diagonal chain with one background cell between consecutive canonical objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2975:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:627:        mode = random.choice((\"vertical\", \"horizontal\", \"diagonal\", \"scatter\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2976:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:635:        elif mode == \"diagonal\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2977:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:19:#    as a sequence of obstacle-modules: approach diagonally on the current side,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2978:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:20:#    skim forward along the obstacle's outer side, then cross diagonally past the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2979:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:22:#    between multiple blockers before its final diagonal tail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2980:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:329:      second-nearest (and possibly third), then keep the final diagonal heading until length runs out.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2981:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:18:#    - D1: the path is now diagonal, so each copy is shifted by (±1, ±1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2982:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:19:#    - D6: the ray no longer ends at the frame; it stops when the next diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2983:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:23:#    notch cell, so the occupied notch identifies one of four diagonals:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2984:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:33:#    the clue ray into sparse diagonal dots, while a 2x2 seed would self-overlap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2985:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:34:#    under unit diagonal shifts and create color-consistency ambiguity. Dominos\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2986:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:35:#    keep the diagonal repetition visually obvious and still allow both 1-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2987:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:42:#      boundary-complete ray needed no further growth. Here a full diagonal clue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2988:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:50:#    a diagonal domino ray and a blocker domino. Exact overlap is forbidden, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2989:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:54:#    In each sample, one ray is already expanded as a long diagonal staircase and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/cesh